 of these rare flowers  that you only find at these Heights  everywhere it's super cool it's  something I could barely even try to  emulate in planet coaster but it's the  kind of feeling that I'm sort of going  for with this area in the Q line oh yeah  I'm pretty happy with it especially the  ground shrubbery is quite good although  in hindsight I really moved the park  border really close to this garden  something which I'm trying to do with  Jaeger horn to make it feel like it  could be part of a real life theme park  is established very hard and straight  borders on the outskirts of the park  which I don't know it's kind of a  limitation  that I'm giving myself because it forces  you to be more creative with how you  approach the edge of the park but it's  also in an attempt to make it seem as  though it could be part of a real park  because where those borders are would be  in real life where another themed area  would be or where some backstage areas  would be I definitely want to get into  some kind of next stage areas for this  park so I think it's quite important to  nail that Disney feeling but at times I  also feel like I put the borders maybe a  bit too close to the park like it's  really difficult to make things look  good if you really have to obviously  place a very very vertical tree line to  block the line of sights to what would  otherwise be backstage areas or empty  grassy planes but you know that's that's  part of the challenge and it's  interesting to try and make forests look  as diverse and dense as possible when in  reality it's just a single tree line  that's meant to make you not see what's  behind it it's something that in real  life I'm also always really fascinated  by in theme parks but yeah that is  basically it for this episode so I'd  like to thank you guys for watching and  I'll leave you with some cinematic  overviews of this ride and just as a  reminder if you wanna donate to stick  thing up kicker and if you want to  support Joey and it's stupid ridiculous  quests to ride Condor for 20 hours in a  row you can find the links to that in  the description as well anyway thanks  for watching and I'll see you in the  next episode which will hopefully be a  bit sooner than usually because it's  going to be summer vacation from now on  so I'll have some more time yay  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

